## Before doing anything

1. Run `git status` and `git log -1` — confirm a clean, up to date `main`
   before editing anything.
2. This app's Supabase project is your own, separate database — never
   assume it's connected to anyone else's Supabase project or data.
3. Deploys happen via `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (GitHub Actions →
   GitHub Pages) whenever you push to `main`, once you've added your
   `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`/`VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` as repository secrets
   (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions) and turned on GitHub
   Pages (Settings → Pages). Until you've done both of those, pushing
   won't produce a working live site yet.

## Architecture

- React + Vite, PWA-first (installable on a phone home screen, works
  offline). Three platform-abstraction modules —
  `src/platform/notifications.js`, `syncQueue.js`, `camera.js` — wrap the
  underlying browser APIs; every other part of the app should call these
  rather than the browser APIs directly, so offline/notification/camera
  behaviour stays consistent everywhere.
- Supabase backend: multi-tenant data model
  (`organisations` → `sites` → `profiles`/`roles`/`groups` → `jobs`).
  Your business is one `organisation` row, which can have more than one
  `site` under it — useful if you run more than one location.
- No table grants directly to the app's public (anon) key. Access control
  is enforced by RLS policies and `security definer` Postgres functions —
  follow this pattern for any new write path rather than granting the
  anon key direct table privileges.
- Offline support via IndexedDB + a foreground flush (not true background
  sync — iOS Safari doesn't support the Background Sync API, so don't
  rely on it; the queue flushes on app load/foreground and `online`
  events instead).

## Hard rules — do not violate these

- Any Supabase SQL change: add a new numbered file in `supabase/` (never
  edit an already-applied one) and actually run it against your live
  project — every migration file here is written idempotently, safe to
  re-run.
- Never put the Supabase **service role key** in `.env` or any
  `VITE_`-prefixed variable — it must never reach the browser. Only
  `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, and
  `VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` belong client-side.
- Every dependency change → regenerate `package-lock.json` in the same
  commit, or `npm ci` fails in the deploy workflow.

